    "file": "../artifacts/01-harbor-dawn-welcome.md",
    "content": "# 01: Harbor Dawn Welcome\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: community welcome\n- Forum: Harbor Dawn\n- Posted: 3 September 2028\n- Author: `mod-samuel`\n- Status: archived\n\n## Artifact\n\nWelcome to Harbor Dawn.\n\nIf you are here because of the Blackwater Floods, start with the practical thread before the grief thread. Food, medication, documents, bedding, transport, childcare, chargers, clean socks. The body gets first vote.\n\nIf you have not slept, say that.\n\nIf you have somewhere safe tonight, say that too. Someone else may need to know safety still exists.\n\nRules:\n\n- No disaster footage without warning.\n- No location speculation about missing people.\n- No fundraising links unless verified by a moderator.\n- No arguing about blame in support threads.\n- No \"everything happens for a reason.\"\n- No one has to be inspiring here.\n\nNightly check-in opens at 21:00.\n\nMorning logistics opens at 07:00.\n\nIf you cannot write a full post, leave a period. Someone will answer.\n\nWe are not here to fix the whole world tonight.\n\nWe are here to get each other to morning.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nHarbor Dawn's early culture was practical before it was sentimental.\n\nThe phrase \"the body gets first vote\" appears repeatedly in later member testimony.\n\nThe rule against blame becomes important once institutional steering is discovered.\n\n"
