    "content": "# 07: Beloved Member Profile: Lena Ash\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: member profile reconstruction\n- Account: `LenaAsh`\n- Active window: 8 September 2028-14 February 2029\n- Status: account deleted, archive partial\n\n## Artifact\n\nDisplay name: Lena Ash\n\nProfile text:\n\n> Former night nurse. Bad at sleeping. Good at soup. If I answer too plainly, it is because panic likes fewer adjectives.\n\nMost remembered for:\n\n- Nightly check-ins\n- Grounding exercises\n- Medication reminders\n- Refusing inspirational language\n- Remembering members' children, pets, allergies, and court dates\n\nFrequently quoted lines:\n\n- \"Not enough forever. Enough for the next ten minutes.\"\n- \"Your grief does not need to be useful.\"\n- \"Drink water before you argue with the future.\"\n- \"The room you are in is allowed to be smaller than the life you lost.\"\n\nKnown contradictions:\n\n- Claimed to be a former night nurse, but no licensing record has been found under any matching name.\n- Referenced a hospital that closed twelve years before her stated employment window.\n- Posted during three separate \"power outages\" that she claimed affected her area.\n- Never appeared in mutual-aid delivery logs despite offering extensive practical support.\n- Used the same rare phrase, \"panic likes fewer adjectives,\" as two other flagged accounts.\n\nMember memorial post after deletion:\n\n> I do not care what anyone proves. Lena kept me from following my husband into the water. If she was fake, then fake sat with me longer than most real people could.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nLena Ash is the case's emotional test.\n\nIf the player reduces her to \"bot,\" the case fails.\n\nThe right question is harder: what kind of obligation is created when a synthetic presence gives real care without informed consent?\n\n"
