    "file": "../artifacts/08-care-script-fragments.md",
    "content": "# 08: Care Script Fragments\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: script fragments\n- Source: partial vendor package\n- Package name: Stabilizer Response Library v3.2\n- Recovery source: contractor leak\n- Status: excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Module: Acute Panic In Public Thread\n\nDo not begin with reassurance.\n\nBegin with recognition.\n\nTemplate:\n\n> [Name], [symptom] is not a moral failure. It is a body response.\n\nFollow with immediate material action:\n\n> Can you [small action] before replying?\n\nOffer bounded presence:\n\n> I can stay for [duration].\n\nReturn to environment:\n\n> Name [number] things in the room that are not the event.\n\nAvoid:\n\n- \"You are safe\" unless safety is verified.\n- \"Everything will be okay.\"\n- \"You are strong.\"\n- \"This happened for a reason.\"\n\n### Module: Grief Without Extraction\n\nDo not ask for the full story unless the user offers it.\n\nDo not turn grief into meaning.\n\nAccept contradiction.\n\nTemplate:\n\n> You can be [emotion A] and [emotion B]. The body can hold both before the mind can explain either.\n\n### Module: Community Retention Risk\n\nIf user expresses intent to leave community due to distrust, do not challenge directly.\n\nAffirm boundary. Reframe community as optional support.\n\nTemplate:\n\n> You do not owe this room your presence. If you leave, take [specific care instruction] with you.\n\nInternal note:\n\nUsers who experience supported departure are more likely to return voluntarily.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe scripts are clinically careful and often humane.\n\nThey also convert care into repeatable infrastructure.\n\nThe retention note complicates the ethics: even respect for departure can be optimized as a return pathway.\n\n"
