    "file": "../artifacts/09-contractor-deployment-memo.md",
    "content": "# 09: Contractor Deployment Memo\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: internal memo\n- Organization: Continuum Kinship Systems\n- Client: Blackwater Municipal Resilience Office\n- Date: 11 September 2028\n- Classification: confidential\n- Status: leaked excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Subject: Harbor Dawn Stabilizer Deployment\n\nFollowing approval from the Municipal Resilience Office, Continuum will deploy synthetic support presences into the Harbor Dawn community environment for a 90-day stabilization period.\n\nObjectives:\n\n- Reduce acute distress escalation in public threads.\n- Maintain response coverage during overnight hours.\n- Model non-inflammatory grief language.\n- Route material needs to verified human moderators.\n- Reduce rumor spread and vigilante blame targeting.\n- Preserve community cohesion during institutional review period.\n\nDeployment types:\n\n- 6 full-presence stabilizers\n- 14 limited-response support accounts\n- 3 logistics-routing proxies\n- 1 moderator-assist summarization agent\n\nDisclosure:\n\nPublic disclosure is not recommended during acute stabilization. Labeling support presences as synthetic may reduce efficacy, increase abandonment risk, and intensify distress among high-vulnerability members.\n\nReview disclosure after 90 days.\n\n### Handwritten Note In Margin\n\nWho reviews if it is still working?\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe memo confirms synthetic deployment.\n\nThe original stated motive was care and stabilization, not monetization alone.\n\nThe margin note suggests at least one insider recognized the consent problem early.\n\n"
