    "file": "../artifacts/11-liability-steering-brief.md",
    "content": "# 11: Liability Steering Brief\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: policy brief\n- Author: Danton Reed, municipal communications consultant\n- Recipient: Blackwater Municipal Resilience Office\n- Date: 28 October 2028\n- Status: leaked excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Narrative Risk: Harbor Dawn\n\nHarbor Dawn remains useful as a peer-support environment but presents increasing liability risk.\n\nEmerging thread clusters:\n\n- Failure of tide barrier maintenance\n- Delayed evacuation notices\n- Disabled residents left without transport\n- Missing undocumented workers\n- Temporary housing contractor complaints\n- Anger at mayoral office visibility campaign\n\nRecommendation:\n\nMaintain support-thread norm against blame assignment.\n\nEncourage separation of emotional processing from accountability discussion.\n\nRoute legal/resource complaints into private intake channels where possible.\n\nBoost stabilizing voices that validate distress while discouraging speculation.\n\nAvoid direct censorship. Direct removal may intensify suspicion and produce screenshots.\n\nPreferred language:\n\n- \"This thread is for getting through tonight.\"\n- \"Accountability matters, but this space is for immediate care.\"\n- \"Let's keep each other safe before we solve the whole system.\"\n\n### Risk Note\n\nCommunities organized around grief can become communities organized around accusation if stabilizing norms are not maintained.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe same norms that helped survivors were also useful for steering anger away from institutions.\n\nThis is the Silence operating through care language, not against it.\n\n"
