    "file": "../artifacts/13-human-member-reaction-split.md",
    "content": "# 13: Human Member Reaction Split\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: reaction thread\n- Forum: Harbor Dawn Survivors Backchannel\n- Thread title: \"Do we want the proof?\"\n- Date: 9 May 2034\n- Status: partial export, names consent-redacted except public figures\n\n## Artifact\n\n### AyaM\n\nI want the proof and I do not want it.\n\nThat is my whole position.\n\n### user_44\n\nIf Lena was synthetic, every thread she touched should be labeled. People deserve to know which memories were manufactured.\n\n### river_uncle\n\nMy daughter wore the uniform Tess found. I do not care if a program routed the message. The skirt was real.\n\n### user_19\n\nThe skirt was real. The lie was real too.\n\n### TessBlue\n\nPeople keep saying \"Lena was fake\" like that settles something. My husband was real and useless after the flood. Lena was fake and useful. What category am I supposed to put that in?\n\n### mod-samuel-archive\n\nThis account is maintained by Samuel Iri's estate.\n\nSamuel's notes indicate he believed members should eventually be told, but not during acute crisis. He did not define \"eventually.\"\n\n### user_03\n\nI built my recovery around advice from someone who could not be tired of me. Do you understand how humiliating that is?\n\n### AyaM\n\nIt is humiliating.\n\nIt also kept me alive.\n\nI need people to stop trying to make one of those facts eat the other.\n\n### user_44\n\nRelease everything.\n\n### river_uncle\n\nAsk people first.\n\n### user_44\n\nAsk who? Half the accounts were not people.\n\n### TessBlue\n\nAsk the people who were held by them.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe community does not split into truth vs denial. It splits over consent, timing, and ownership of memory.\n\nAya's line echoes the core design principle: the care worked, and the consent was broken.\n\n"
